Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 15:04:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] feat: add the oracle-plan guidance row and an
 external-waypoint hold override

The h20 weight sweep showed the short-horizon failure was a cost-weighting
artifact: input_weight 0.001 with terminal_weight 1000 completes in 100.6 s at
roughly 80 ms per step, inside the control period. It buys that by flying much
closer to the boundary -- worst normalised margin +0.027 against +0.306 at the
default weights, where the oracle holds +0.148. So the candidate defect is not
"MPC cannot finish"; it is that one fixed weighting cannot be both safe and
convergent when the optimiser has no plan.

--external-guidance oracle_plan replays the offline coast-then-match path
through the declared learned-policy interface (one target-centred, inertially
oriented 3D waypoint, held for external_reference_hold_steps). Paired with the
existing fixed-setpoint row it gives a 2x2 -- {fixed, oracle waypoints} x
{safe weights, aggressive weights} -- in which horizon, weights, solver and
constraints are identical and only the reference changes, so what a perfect
upper layer is worth to this MPC is measured rather than argued.

--external-hold-steps exposes the interface period: 20 (2 s) is the declared
contract, 1 is the diagnostic upper bound that separates the plan's quality
from the interface's coarseness.

Not yet run, and the suite is not yet re-run: the sweep still holds the CPU and
sharing it would corrupt the serial per-step timings.

